{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3319","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3319","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3319\",\"parent_revision\":\"ac4ee0ccc080edf3e2648dbc89a207932b435c499595496a1779d4f1019c8ff3\",\"root_revision\":\"ac4ee0ccc080edf3e2648dbc89a207932b435c499595496a1779d4f1019c8ff3\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nObserved 2026-08-28/29 while running `/dh:work-backlog-item work --auto #3268`. #3268's own RT-ICA assessment scoped this exact problem OUT of that plan, stating: \\\"task-worker.md's own Identity (SAM-task-plan executor) mismatches its ad-hoc dispatch use in close/start.md, groom/error.md, groom-drift.md \u2014 filed as a separate follow-up backlog item, not in scope here.\\\" That claim is false: a full-text and title search of the GitHub tracker (`gh issue list --search \\\"task-worker Identity\\\"`, `\\\"task-worker dispatch sites\\\"`, `\\\"groom-drift quick post-planning dispatch\\\"`) turns up no matching item. The finding was never actually filed \u2014 only asserted as filed.\\n\\nThe mismatch itself is real and verified directly against source:\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md`'s `## Identity` and `## Step 1 \u2014 Read the Task (profile lookup only)` (lines 12-33) unconditionally require a plan address + task ID in the dispatch prompt (`{plan} --task {task_id}` or bare `P{N}/T{M}`), and immediately call `sam_task(action='read')` against that plan/task \u2014 returning `STATUS: BLOCKED` if the call errors.\\n\\nAt least one dispatch site in `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/error.md:18` invokes `Agent(subagent_type=\\\"dh:task-worker\\\", prompt=\\\"Review the session transcript for the failed agent...\\\")` \u2014 a free-form diagnostic errand carrying **no plan address and no task ID whatsoever**. Under task-worker's own Step 1, this dispatch has nothing to parse and no real `sam_task` to read, so the agent's documented behavior (block on `sam_task` failure) is undefined/unreliable for this call shape.\\n\\nThree further sites carry the same ad-hoc-dispatch shape and need the same check: `groom/groom-drift.md:36` and `:65` (haiku agents spawned as `dh:task-worker` for drift-assessment sub-tasks, not SAM plan tasks), and `close/start.md` Step 5.6 (the #3268-fixed verification-agent dispatch, which passes `item_ref` + a plan address but no specific task ID within that plan \u2014 still not a real SAM task node).\\n\\n### Suggested scope\\nFor each of the four sites (`groom/error.md:18`, `groom-drift.md:36`, `groom-drift.md:65`, `close/start.md` Step 5.6) plus `quick/start.md:110,179` and `work/post-planning.md:14` (same `dh:task-worker` name used for a real per-task SAM dispatch loop there \u2014 confirm that one is NOT a mismatch, since it does carry real task IDs): either (a) give task-worker.md's Step 1 an explicit branch for a no-task/ad-hoc dispatch shape that skips the `sam_task(read)` requirement, or (b) redirect these ad-hoc call sites to a plain `general-purpose`/blank-canvas agent instead of `dh:task-worker`, since `dh:task-worker`'s whole identity is built around the SAM claim/complete lifecycle these calls never invoke.\\n\\n### Evidence\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md:12-33`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/error.md:18`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/groom-drift.md:36,65`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/close/start.md` Step 5.6 (post-#3268 fix)\\n- Backlog item #3268, RT-ICA Assumptions to confirm, item (b) \u2014 the false \\\"already filed\\\" claim this item corrects\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Not specified\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"c1986cbb354b65638c68ff66b521d3a4dde2afa329ca00d85612cbb3ed58a8b3\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRZ5Hqw\"}"}